  "reading": {
   "title": "Hafsa remembers Isparta",
   "text": "When Hafsa was a girl, she lived in a small village near Isparta. The village was very quiet. There was a big garden behind her house, and there were many roses in it. Isparta is famous for roses, and the whole town smelled sweet in May.\n\nHafsa was a shy child, but she was never bored. She was always busy. In summer she was in the orchard with the neighbors, and they were happy to pick apples. In winter the mountains were white with snow. Her school was not far, and her teacher was very kind.\n\nToday Hafsa lives in the United States. Her son Emre asks, \"Were you happy in the village?\" She smiles. \"Yes, I was. We weren't rich, but we were lucky.\"",
